Inert-edit probe -- FILED EVIDENCE, not a re-runnable gate.
==========================================================

Run 2026-11-16 on `claude/pending-task-vg2afd` at 8d2b73c8, by
`python3 tools/mutate.py --probe-only`, which sweeps a detached git worktree
so this tree is never dirty. It replaces, whole, the run of 2026-09-16 at
d92c4e1 (84 OK, 1 FAIL, `contract_build`), which git history keeps.

WHAT IT ANSWERS. `tools/mutate.py` reports a mutation score, and that score is
vacuous if any test in the suite detects the EDIT rather than the DEFECT:
such a test kills every mutant and the sweep reports 100%. `EXCLUDED_TESTS`
names the ones that do, and since 2026-09-27 `mutate.py` runs this probe
before every sweep and refuses to report a score when the set is wrong.

THE EDIT. One comment appended at EOF of `src/utils.c`, moving no line number:

    /* mutate.py inert-edit probe: behaviourally inert */

The probe refuses if the edit does not build, so a stale binary cannot pass
for a clean result. It reads meson's totals, and refuses if there are none, so
a suite that stopped early cannot pass either. A test that fails in the full
suite is run again alone, still under the edit, so a flake under load is not
counted as a detector.

THE RESULT, the probe's output verbatim:

    sweeping a worktree at /tmp/cyanrip-mutate-ym8q3e9g -- this checkout is untouched
    inert-edit probe: a comment appended at EOF of src/utils.c
      meson's totals under the edit: Ok 173, Expected Fail 0, Fail 1, Unexpected Pass 0, Skipped 0, Timeout 0
      tests that detect the edit: ['contract_build']
      EXCLUDED_TESTS is exactly the set: ['contract_build']

All 174 tests ran. The one failure is `contract_build`, which hashes src/
into the provider contract's source anchor and so fails on any byte changed
there. **The exclusion list is still complete**, 89 tests after the last run.

WHY THIS IS THE FIRST RUN SINCE 2026-09-16. The probe that `mutate.py` runs
read a failing test's name up to the first `:`, the way meson printed it on
2026-09-16 (`images - cyanrip:contract_build`). Meson 1.3.2 prints
`cyanrip:images / contract_build`, which that read as `images /
contract_build`, so the probe's first run, at 63ef6ade earlier the same day,
refused on its own exclusion:

    tests that detect the edit: ['images / contract_build']
    REFUSING: ['images / contract_build'] fail on an edit that changes no behaviour, ...
    REFUSING: EXCLUDED_TESTS names ['contract_build'], which no longer fail on the edit. ...

907461eb reads the name after the last ` / ` and refuses a name that `meson
introspect --tests` does not list; a run at 907461eb then passed without
totals, which 8d2b73c8 added before this run.

RE-RUN IT DELIBERATELY, not on a schedule: it is a full build plus the whole
suite in a worktree.

    python3 tools/mutate.py --probe-only
    # expect: EXCLUDED_TESTS is exactly the set, with meson's totals above it
